Sval: clearing a jar forgets the client certificates chosen in it

A remembered choice of client certificate is kept by host and origin
attributes, and ClientAuthRememberCleaner had no deleteByOriginAttributes,
so deleteDataFromOriginAttributesPattern left it. A deleted Workspace's jar
is cleared that way, and its choices stayed in the profile for a jar that
no longer exists.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.sys.mjs b/toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.sys.mjs
index 39ea7660e4..0abd82fcf7 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.sys.mjs
@@ -1830,6 +1830,30 @@ const ClientAuthRememberCleaner = {
       .forEach(({ entryKey }) => cars.forgetRememberedDecision(entryKey));
   },
 
